One-time setup that Terraform itself cannot do (chicken-and-egg):

1. State bucket
   aws s3api create-bucket --bucket notif-system-tfstate --region eu-west-2 \
     --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=eu-west-2
   aws s3api put-bucket-versioning --bucket notif-system-tfstate --versioning-configuration Status=Enabled

2. Permissions for the IAM user whose keys CI uses (scoped to notif-system-* resources).
   Attached via a group: inline user policies are capped at 2048 bytes total and
   a user can hold at most 10 managed policies, group policies count against neither.
   ACCT=$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text)
   aws iam create-policy --policy-name NotifSystemTerraform \
     --policy-document file://terraform/bootstrap/ci-user-policy.json
   aws iam create-group --group-name notif-system-ci
   aws iam attach-group-policy --group-name notif-system-ci \
     --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::$ACCT:policy/NotifSystemTerraform
   aws iam add-user-to-group --group-name notif-system-ci --user-name <ci-user>

3. Updating the policy later (IAM keeps up to 5 versions; delete an old one if that limit hits)
   aws iam create-policy-version --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::$ACCT:policy/NotifSystemTerraform \
     --policy-document file://terraform/bootstrap/ci-user-policy.json --set-as-default
